s\\n\\n Test Files  1 failed | 158 passed (159)\\n      Tests  2 failed | 3523 passed | 3 skipped (3528)\\n   Start at  17:24:50\\n   Duration  153.09s (transform 11.10s, setup 0ms, import 21.26s, tests 1640.89s, environment 19ms)) failed in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts (normal/signal/crash cleanup paths). Posted MUST-FIX inline review on PR #586 and transitioned task to needs_work for fix cycle.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGXVE92ER5MGW40VNN3ZZR0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:29:48.579Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Fix cycle 1 started from PR #586 review feedback. Investigating regression in ralph session-budget integration tests and pending_review handling path.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGY1Z9AG1WYEX8CW0VMX05K\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:33:22.602Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Fix cycle 1 changes:\\n- Fixed task loading under KSPEC_SPEC_DIR override: loadAllTasks now treats spec-dir override as spec-only mode (same behavior as shadow mode) to prevent scanning parent directories and pulling unrelated temp task files.\\n- Fixed ralph pending-review escalation command from deprecated `task set-automation` to `task set --automation needs_review --reason ...`.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npm run build && npx vitest run tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts (15/15 passing)\\n- npm test (159 files, 3525 tests passing)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJHAD8E2QTA99YTNYCFCR9AT\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix: Truncate oversized ACP prompt payloads\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Ralph subagent and worker prompts embed raw JSON.stringify() of task/spec/session data inline. For large payloads (tasks with many notes, large specs), the resulting JSON-RPC line exceeds the Codex Rust binary read buffer, causing 'agent_client_protocol::rpc: failed to parse incoming message'. The parser receives a partial fragment and fails. Observed on the review subagent path, but the worker prompt has the same vulnerability.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-subagent-spawning\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"PR #590 reviewed and merged at head 690d0648\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"ralph\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T05:09:15.330Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:41:10.956Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:01:39.719Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:01:41.319Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJHAEBJXW166DHNWR5EMFZSF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T05:09:51.326Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Root Cause: Ralph prompts embed raw JSON.stringify() of task/spec/session data inline. For large payloads, the JSON-RPC line exceeds the Codex Rust binary read buffer causing parse failures. Approach: 32KB total prompt budget with largest-first truncation. Truncated sections show a blockquote notice with CLI fetch command and compact identity summary. Changes: (1) subagent.ts — SUBAGENT_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES, formatJsonSection(), truncatePromptIfNeeded(), compactSummary(). Updated buildSubagentPrompt(). (2) ralph.ts — Updated buildTaskWorkPrompt() with same helpers. (3) ralph/index.ts — Exported new helpers. (4) tests/ralph.test.ts — 14 new tests covering formatJsonSection, truncatePromptIfNeeded, and end-to-end buildSubagentPrompt truncation. (5) Spec ac-10 updated to reflect truncation behavior.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJMZYZR08RD00DZW1ACTRV0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T17:33:28.440Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Codex review on PR #590 found 2 MUST-FIX issues: (1) session-budget-integration test regression — 4/15 fail on branch vs 15/15 on main, though may be pre-existing flakiness tracked in @01KJGDR9; (2) AC annotation coverage gap for @ralph-subagent-spawning (9 of 13 ACs missing test annotations, mostly pre-existing).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJN05R8MPWDZRFTJFZ9NBVW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T17:33:35.369Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Codex PR review posted on #590 (pullrequestreview-3870620687). Two inline MUST-FIX comments:\\n1. src/ralph/subagent.ts:288 — session-budget-integration regression (4 test failures on branch, passes on main). Likely related to flaky timeout issue tracked in @01KJGDR9.\\n2. tests/ralph.test.ts:1680 — AC annotation coverage gap: only ac-2,9,10,11 annotated out of ac-1..13. Mostly pre-existing, not introduced by this PR.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJN2P73CJ748CQMEXTHA2J7\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T17:34:57.764Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Execution context:\\n- Background: PR #590 failed review due to session-budget-integration regressions and missing AC annotations for @ralph-subagent-spawning.\\n- Scope: stabilize session-budget integration behavior and add missing AC annotations for ac-1,3,4,5,6,7,8,12,13.\\n- Files: tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts, tests/ralph.test.ts, and minimal production code only if required by failing behavior.\\n- Verification: npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts; npm test -- tests/ralph.test.ts; npm test; kspec validate.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJPJ7HY6PW6N2N0F2XW82VB\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:00:55.615Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed MUST-FIX findings.\\n- Restored ralph timeout escalation command to current CLI shape: task set --automation needs_review --reason (replacing deprecated set-automation call).\\n- Added explicit AC annotations and integration coverage for @ralph-subagent-spawning ac-1,3,4,5,6,7,8,12,13 in ralph-context-refresh/ralph tests.\\n- Added mock ACP support for reviewer kickback path (MOCK_ACP_NEEDS_WORK_TASK) and verified task transitions to needs_work.\\n- Fixed session-budget integration harness isolation by removing KSPEC_SPEC_DIR override (it widened task discovery to /tmp and pulled unrelated pending_review fixtures).\\nVerification:\\n- npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts tests/ralph.test.ts (pass, 157 tests)\\n- npm test (fails in unrelated tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout; reproduced in isolation).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJQ8NTKQ46V5D7CMFTWTJA1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:13:11.123Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Codex PR review posted (pullrequestreview-3870655818). MUST-FIX: PR CI test shard 2 fails in tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts (assertions at lines 482 and 512). Root cause from CI logs: reviewer status/transition subprocess paths rely on bare 'kspec' and return null status in Actions context. Fix CLI invocation path in status-check helpers, then re-run CI.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJQVHMGYH4HCA79V7NEX8YM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:23:29.424Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Addressed PR review follow-up MUST-FIX items.\\n- Replaced hardcoded 'kspec' subprocess usage in ralph status/transition checks with portable Node CLI invocation (process.execPath + dist CLI path, optional KSPEC_CLI_PATH override).\\n- Hardened ralph-context-refresh integration assertions to verify task state transitions (completed/needs_work) instead of brittle log-string contracts.\\nVerification:\\n- npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts tests/ralph.test.ts (pass)\\n- npm run test:shard2 (pass; 1361 tests).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJRTTNYMD3QJ8W9QQYQZ8ZF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:40:34.494Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 6] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #590 is merge-conflicting with main (mergeable CONFLICTING / mergeStateStatus DIRTY). Rebase/resolve conflicts and rerun CI on latest HEAD.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJSCAPYPR6V25NXGCFQVF0Y\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:50:07.967Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Rebased fix/truncate-oversized-acp-prompts onto origin/main to resolve PR #590 merge conflict flagged by review subagent. No manual conflict edits were required. Re-verified after rebase:\\n- npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts tests/ralph.test.ts (pass)\\n- npm run test:shard2 (pass)\\nPushed rebased branch with --force-with-lease.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJGJ17SR1GSXNK90DXKY4CR\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix merge driver non-interactive flag and improve conflict resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**Background**: Shadow branch diverged (170 local vs 260 remote commits). During merge, the merge driver was registered without --non-interactive, causing it to hang on stdin when conflicts were detected. This left files unmerged (ours version only), silently losing 12 task completions, notes, and remote-side spec changes.\\n\\n**Already done (this session):**\\n1. Diagnosed root cause: git config had `kspec merge-driver %O %A %B %P` but needed `--non-interactive` flag\\n2. Fixed local git config to include --non-interactive\\n3. Performed isolated rebase in /tmp worktree to produce correctly merged state\\n4. Applied corrected data as patch commit on kspec-meta (no force push needed)\\n5. Restored all 12 lost task completions with notes, verified 705 tasks intact\\n6. Marked 37 stale active sessions as abandoned, compacted all sessions (383MB reclaimed)\\n7. Created backup branches: kspec-meta-backup-2026-02-28 (pre-merge local), kspec-remote-pre-merge (pre-merge remote)\\n\\n**Still to do:**\\n1. Fix shadow.ts registration — ensure kspec init/setup always registers driver with --non-interactive\\n2. Add TTY detection fallback — merge driver should auto-detect when stdin is not a TTY and default to non-interactive mode (defense in depth)\\n3. Fix exit code behavior — in non-interactive mode, exit 0 even with conflicts (they're auto-resolved with ours-defaults + comments). Exit 1 breaks git rebase.\\n4. Improve notes array merging — when both sides modify notes, union by timestamp instead of picking one side. Notes are append-only logs.\\n5. Resolve inbox item about .kspec-agents-hash auto-resolution (01KJDFFJ)\\n6. Restore 8 lost notes on @01KJDQ11 (observations slug fix task) — local had detailed work log that was replaced by remote's 3 automated notes\\n7. Consider timestamp-aware conflict resolution for status fields (task state has natural ordering)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@yaml-merge-driver\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #601. Fixed merge driver: (1) shadow.ts validates/fixes stale config missing --non-interactive, (2) TTY detection auto-enables non-interactive when stdin is not TTY, (3) non-interactive mode exits 0 even with conflicts per spec ac-10. All tests pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"infra\",\n      \"bug\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:15:57.681Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:31:00.151Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:37:34.567Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:58:33.763Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJGJSC1QET01A4DV0TR5WYD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:16:22.402Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Session work completed (2026-02-28):\\n\\nRoot cause: merge driver registered without --non-interactive flag. When git invoked it on conflicting YAML files, it attempted interactive resolution via readline on unavailable stdin, hanging indefinitely. The ours file was never written with merged content, so git used unmodified ours version — silently losing remote-side changes.\\n\\nKey finding: merge driver has NO timestamp awareness — purely structural 3-way merge. For notes (append-only), it picks one side instead of unioning both.\\n\\nRebase approach worked: 170 local commits rebased onto 260 remote in isolated /tmp worktree. Auto-continue script handled non-YAML conflicts. All 169 commits applied. Result: 705 tasks with both sides preserved.\\n\\nOne data loss: Task @01KJDQ11 notes — 8 local notes replaced by 3 remote (ours-bias in rebase context). Backup branches available: kspec-meta-backup-2026-02-28 (local), kspec-remote-pre-merge (remote).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJH0155QWRXXC31YDA31HCJ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:23:36.357Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Refined scope — 3 code changes needed:\\n\\n1. src/parser/shadow.ts — Ensure all code paths that register merge.kspec.driver include --non-interactive. Audit initShadowBranch and any other registration points.\\n\\n2. src/cli/commands/merge-driver.ts — Two fixes:\\n   a. TTY detection: if process.stdin.isTTY is false, auto-enable non-interactive mode regardless of flag. Defense-in-depth so driver never hangs.\\n   b. Exit code: in non-interactive mode, exit 0 even with conflicts (line 536). Currently exits 1 which breaks git rebase. The spec ac-10 already says exit 0.\\n\\n3. src/merge/arrays.ts (mergeUlidArrays or equivalent) — Notes arrays should be union-merged by ULID, not fall through to scalar conflict. Spec ac-5 says 'notes never conflict' but the implementation doesn't match when arrays differ.\\n\\nItems from original description already done: lost notes on @01KJDQ11 restored, inbox item @01KJDFFJ is separate scope, timestamp-aware status resolution is a future enhancement.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHKEVS5G77Z1WYPKBHG165\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:34:12.986Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation changes (3 files):\\n\\n1. src/parser/shadow.ts — When existing merge driver config found in catch block, now validates --non-interactive flag is present. If missing (legacy registration), re-registers with --non-interactive. Ensures no stale config can cause hangs.\\n\\n2. src/cli/commands/merge-driver.ts (line 514) — Added TTY detection fallback: nonInteractive defaults to true when process.stdin.isTTY is false. Defense-in-depth so driver never hangs even if --non-interactive flag is somehow missing.\\n\\n3. src/cli/commands/merge-driver.ts (lines 534-536) — Non-interactive mode now always exits 0 regardless of conflicts. Per spec ac-10, conflicts are written as YAML comments and exit 0 prevents git from falling back to text merge (which corrupts YAML). Interactive mode retains exit 1 for unresolved conflicts.\\n\\nTests updated: 4 existing tests that expected exit code 1 for non-interactive conflicts now expect exit 0. All 12 merge-driver-cli tests pass.\\n\\nNote: Array merge (notes union by ULID) was already correctly implemented — no changes needed there. The spec ac-5 behavior was already working.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":695003262},"formatted_output":"Total output lines: 13831\n\n[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB01TASK100000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Set up TypeScript project with Zod\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Initialize the kspec CLI project:\\n- TypeScript + Node.js project structure\\n- Zod for schema validation\\n- Build tooling (tsup or similar)\\n- Basic package.json with bin entry\\n\",\n    \"derivation\": \"manual\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Bootstrap complete - project fully set up and self-hosting\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"foundation\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.951Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:00:00Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:20:00Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ953HRYWJ0W4XEG6J9FB\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:00:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Bootstrap approach: Used parallel subagents working in git worktrees.\\nOne agent wrote the spec (bootstrap-spec branch), another wrote the\\nparser (bootstrap-parser branch). Branches merged after alignment.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ95AMA2JDAN9RMJ1Q2R3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:10:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Tech stack chosen:\\n- TypeScript + Node.js (ESM modules)\\n- Zod for schema validation\\n- Commander for CLI framework\\n- js-yaml for YAML parsing\\n- ulid for ID generation\\n- Vitest for testing\\n- chalk for colored output\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ95AAPYJAY169ERRFSNH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:15:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Project structure (~1,500 lines TypeScript):\\n- src/schema/ - Zod schemas (common, spec, task)\\n- src/parser/ - YAML loading and file management\\n- src/cli/ - Command handlers (tasks, task)\\n- tests/ - Vitest test suite\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ95A6VKGXGZ84R6TQ517\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:18:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Schema alignment fix: Initial mismatch between spec and parser\\n(parallel development). Fixed by making created_at optional with\\ndefault, adding description field. First real issue resolved\\nusing the self-hosting system.\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB02TASK110000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-ulid-generation\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement ULID generation and resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement ULID handling:\\n- Generate new ULIDs (use ulid library)\\n- Shorten ULIDs for display (first 6+ chars)\\n- Resolve short ULIDs to full (with ambiguity detection)\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ulid-system\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit confirmed: implemented during bootstrap\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:49.872Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:51.210Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB03TASK120000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-slug-system\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement slug management and resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement slug handling:\\n- Validate slug format (lowercase, alphanumeric, hyphens)\\n- Build slug-to-ULID index\\n- Resolve slugs to ULIDs\\n- Detect and report duplicates\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@slug-system\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit confirmed: implemented during bootstrap\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:52.551Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:53.903Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB04TASK130000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-reference-resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement @reference resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement reference resolution:\\n- Parse @ prefix to extract identifier\\n- Try slug lookup first, then ULID prefix\\n- Report unresolved references\\n- Handle ambiguous references\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@reference-system\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented ReferenceIndex with dynamic ULID shortening, proper error handling, and reference validation\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-ulid-generation\",\n      \"@task-slug-system\",\n      \"@task-yaml-loading\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:23:21.734Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:31:29.287Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZD4BHZFA5E4FQ0182JKXRA\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:23:24.096Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Starting work on reference resolution. User noted that 6-char ULID prefixes aren't granular enough since ULIDs created at similar times share timestamp prefixes. Will implement dynamic prefix expansion for uniqueness.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZDJZRTZ6D3QWY1X7FZH5BG\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:31:23.547Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented reference resolution system:\\n\\n1. Created ReferenceIndex class (src/parser/refs.ts) with:\\n   - Slug index (slug → ULID mapping)\\n   - ULID index for direct lookups\\n   - resolve() method with proper error handling (not_found, ambiguous, duplicate_slug)\\n   - shortUlid() for dynamic prefix computation (min 8 chars, expands for uniqueness)\\n   - validateRefs() to find all broken references in spec\\n\\n2. Updated CLI (src/cli/commands/task.ts):\\n   - All task commands now use ReferenceIndex for lookups\\n   - Better error messages showing ambiguous matches with short ULIDs + slugs\\n   - Output uses dynamic short ULIDs\\n\\n3. Added comprehensive tests for:\\n   - Slug resolution\\n   - Full/short ULID resolution\\n   - Ambiguity detection\\n   - Duplicate slug detection\\n   - Reference validation\\n\\nThe 8-char minimum prefix gets into the random portion of ULIDs, fixing the issue where items created at similar times would have identical 6-char prefixes.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZE05XQQGTDKMRZ2S0BPVNH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:38:35.832Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Additional follow-up: Updated all CLI locations to use dynamic shortUlid():\\n\\n- output.ts: formatTaskRef, formatTask, formatTaskList now accept optional ReferenceIndex\\n- tasks.ts: All commands (list, ready, next, blocked, in-progress) build index and pass to formatters\\n- task.ts: task add command builds index including new task for accurate short ULID\\n\\nShort IDs now dynamically expand based on uniqueness within the spec. Items created in the same timestamp batch (e.g., 01JHNKAB*) show 10+ chars, while items with unique prefixes show the minimum 8 chars.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB06TASK200000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-zod-schemas\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Define Zod schemas for spec items\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Define comprehensive Zod schemas:\\n- BaseItem schema (common fields)\\n- Type-specific schemas (feature, requirement, etc.)\\n- Task schema (with task-specific fields)\\n- Nested schemas (status, acceptance_criteria, etc.)\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@zod-schema\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit confirmed: implemented during bootstrap\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"schema\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:55.247Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:56.562Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB07TASK210000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-yaml-loading\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement YAML file loading\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement spec loading:\\n- Parse manifest (kynetic.yaml)\\n- Handle includes (load referenced files)\\n- Support glob patterns in includes\\n- Build unified item collection\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@file-structure\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Full spec loading implemented with recursive item extraction, glob includes, and ULID migration\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-zod-schemas\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"schema\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:04:25.740Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:15:14.678Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZCN7G9WB9J852E0X90JDXX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:15:08.426Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented full YAML spec loading:\\n- Added LoadedSpecItem interface for source file tracking\\n- Implemented expandIncludePattern() with glob support (*.yaml patterns)\\n- Added extractItemsFromRaw() for recursive nested item extraction from modules/features/requirements\\n- Implemented loadAllItems() to build unified item collection from manifest + includes\\n- Added findItemByRef() and findAnyItemByRef() for item lookup\\n- Fixed YAML syntax error in core.yaml (unquoted @references)\\n- Created ULID migration script (scripts/migrate-ulids.ts) and migrated 59 invalid ULIDs to valid Crockford base32\\n- Added comprehensive tests for spec loading (extractItemsFromRaw, findItemByRef, expandIncludePattern, loadAllItems integration)\\n- All 45 tests passing\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB08TASK220000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-item-indexing\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Build item index for queries\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Build queryable index:\\n- Index by ULID (primary key)\\n- Index by slug (lookup)\\n- Index by type (filtering)\\n- Enable efficient lookups\\n\",\n    \"derivation\": \"manual\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented ItemIndex with multi-criteria queries and CLI commands for item list/get/types/tags\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-yaml-loading\",\n      \"@task-reference-resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"schema\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:32:24.893Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:36:45.665Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZVM219JSJ3DCGZDK3ADVTG\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:36:38.698Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented ItemIndex class (src/parser/items.ts) with:\\n- Indexes by type, tag, status (task status, maturity, implementation)\\n- Multi-criteria query() method supporting: type, tags, allTags, status, maturity, implementation, hasFields, fieldEquals, titleContains\\n- Pagination via queryPaginated()\\n- Convenience methods: getByType(), getByTag(), getTasksByStatus(), getByMaturity(), getByImplementation()\\n- Stats: getTypes(), getTags(), getTypeCounts(), getTagCounts()\\n\\nAdded CLI commands (src/cli/commands/item.ts):\\n- kspec item list [filters] - list items with --type, --status, --maturity, --tag, --has, --search\\n- kspec item get <ref> - show item details\\n- kspec item types - show type counts\\n- kspec item tags - show tag counts\\n\\nAdded buildIndexes() helper to build both ReferenceIndex and ItemIndex together.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB10TASK300000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-schema-validation\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement schema validation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement Zod-based validation:\\n- Validate each item against schema\\n- Collect all errors (don't fail fast)\\n- Format errors with item context\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@validation-modes\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented kspec validate with schema, reference, and orphan checks\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-zod-schemas\",\n      \"@task-yaml-loading\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"validation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:44:44.224Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:48:11.313Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZW902C94QSBJHMVQAJER00\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:48:04.813Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented schema validation module (src/parser/validate.ts):\\n- Schema validation: validates manifests, task files, and spec files against Zod schemas\\n- Reference validation: checks all @references resolve (reuses validateRefs from refs.ts)\\n- Orphan detection: finds items not referenced (excludes tasks/modules as entry points)\\n\\nCLI commands:\\n- kspec validate - run all checks\\n- kspec validate --schema - schema only\\n- kspec validate --refs - refs only\\n- kspec validate --orphans - orphans only\\n- kspec validate --strict - treat orphans as errors\\n- kspec lint - alias for validate\\n\\nValidation found real issues in kspec's own spec:\\n- 4 broken refs to @milestone-self-hosting (doesn't exist)\\n- 72 orphaned spec items (requirements nested under features - may be false positives)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB11TASK310000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-ref-validation\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement reference validation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Validate all @references:\\n- Scan all relationship fields\\n- Check each reference resolves\\n- Report broken references with context\\n- Warn on deprecated targets\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ref-validation\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented as part of schema validation task. Core functionality complete: @ prefix parsing, slug/ULID resolution, error reporting. Deprecated target warnings deferred (minor enhancement).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-reference-resolution\",\n      \"@task-item-indexing\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"validation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.953Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:57:21.544Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:57:21.544Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZWSRT1B1RJRDDX48FF62F0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:57:14.434Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Reference validation was implemented as part of @01JHNKAB10 (schema validation task). The implementation covers:\\n\\n1. ✅ Parse @ prefix to extract identifier\\n2. ✅ Slug lookup, then ULID prefix match resolution\\n3. ✅ Error reporting for unresolved/ambiguous references\\n4. ⏳ Deprecated target warnings - not implemented (requires deprecated field on items, minor enhancement)\\n\\nCLI: kspec validate --refs works and successfully found 4 broken @milestone-self-hosting refs which were fixed in @01KEZWDH.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KEZWVQ5PTQY5V5F6ZTSE3Z9S\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-deprecated-warnings\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Warn on deprecated targets in reference validation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Add warnings when references point to deprecated items:\\n- Add deprecated field to item schema (or use implementation: deprecated)\\n- Check resolved targets for deprecated status\\n- Report as warnings (not errors) in validation output\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ref-validation\",\n    \"derivation\": \"manual\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented deprecation warnings in reference validation with full test coverage\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-ref-validation\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"complexity\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"post-mvp\",\n      \"validation\",\n      \"enhancement\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:58:00.000Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:23:07.151Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:23:07.151Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KF7ZBSG8XMZ63HS2553N0DV1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:15:57.576Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Found current implementation. Spec items can be deprecated via:\\n1. maturity: 'deprecated' status\\n2. deprecated_in: <version> field\\n\\nPlan:\\n1. Add new warning type to RefValidationError (currently only has errors)\\n2. Modify validateRefs() to check resolved items for deprecation\\n3. Return warnings separately from errors in ValidationResult\\n4. Update CLI output to show warnings distinctly from errors\\n5. Add tests for deprecated reference warnings\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KF7ZRQ0QMBFSTPF5WH11Y3Z8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:23:01.015Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete and tested:\\n\\n1. Added RefValidationWarning type for deprecation warnings in src/parser/refs.ts\\n2. Created isDeprecated() helper that checks both maturity: 'deprecated' and deprecated_in fields\\n3. Modified validateRefs() to return RefValidationResult with errors and warnings arrays\\n4. Updated ValidationResult in src/parser/validate.ts to include refWarnings field\\n5. Updated CLI output in src/cli/commands/validate.ts to display warnings in yellow with ⚠ symbol\\n6. Added 3 comprehensive tests for deprecated reference warnings:\\n   - Test for maturity: deprecated\\n   - Test for deprecated_in field\\n   - Test ensuring no warnings for active references\\n7. Updated all existing validateRefs tests to handle new return structure\\n\\nAll tests pass (432 tests). Feature works correctly when running 'kspec validate --refs'.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB12TASK320000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-validation-output\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement validation output formatting\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Format validation results:\\n- Human-readable output (default)\\n- JSON output (--json flag)\\n- Exit codes based on severity\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@validation-output\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented as part of schema validation. Human-readable and JSON output both working.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-schema-validation\",\n      \"@t…252144 tokens truncated…ould display AC count in dry-run output  496ms\\n     ✓ should include ac_count in JSON output  814ms\\n     ✓ should show complexity warning for specs with >5 ACs  1153ms\\n     ✓ should show complexity warning in dry-run for specs with >5 ACs  1271ms\\n     ✓ should show Quick Commands for active task  333ms\\n     ✓ should add acceptance criterion with auto-generated ID  319ms\\n     ✓ should add acceptance criterion with custom ID  322ms\\n     ✓ should reject duplicate AC ID  319ms\\n     ✓ should update acceptance criterion  488ms\\n     ✓ should remove acceptance criterion  631ms\\n     ✓ should handle YAML special characters correctly  485ms\\n     ✓ should auto-increment AC IDs correctly  621ms\\n     ✓ should return JSON output  312ms\\n     ✓ should show dry-run output without deleting  641ms\\n     ✓ should delete task with --force  658ms\\n     ✓ should show derive hint after item set  320ms\\n     ✓ should show AC count in alignment guidance for task with spec_ref  987ms\\n     ✓ should show spec context when starting task with spec_ref  795ms\\n     ✓ should not show spec context when starting task without spec_ref  330ms\\n     ✓ should suppress spec context in JSON mode  645ms\\n     ✓ should show commit guidance with spec_ref after task complete  823ms\\n     ✓ should warn about spec gap when no spec_ref  655ms\\n     ✓ should not show guidance in JSON mode  665ms\\n     ✓ should add a note to a spec item  304ms\\n     ✓ should add a note with author  313ms\\n     ✓ should list all notes for a spec item  463ms\\n     ✓ should show \\\"No notes\\\" when spec item has no notes  308ms\\n     ✓ should output notes as JSON  325ms\\n     ✓ should list relationships to an item (reverse lookup)  312ms\\n     ✓ should filter relationships by type  459ms\\n     ✓ should delete a relationship  458ms\\n     ✓ should update children when cascade accepted  457ms\\n     ✓ should not update children when cascade rejected  446ms\\n     ✓ should use inbox text as description by default  454ms\\n     ✓ should use custom description when --description flag provided  447ms\\n     ✓ should handle empty description flag  454ms\\n     ✓ should replace item content while preserving ULID and timestamp  439ms\\n     ✓ should preserve tags when only updating content  568ms\\n     ✓ should add new tags to existing tags  571ms\\n     ✓ should not duplicate tags  582ms\\n     ✓ should support --clear-tags to replace all tags  575ms\\n     ✓ should append note to existing text with separator  581ms\\n     ✓ should support multiple notes  745ms\\n     ✓ should preserve tags when adding notes  592ms\\n     ✓ should convert inbox item to observation with default type  603ms\\n     ✓ should convert inbox item with explicit type override  587ms\\n     ✓ should preserve workflow reference when converting from inbox  446ms\\n     ✓ should fail with invalid type when using --from-inbox  448ms\\n     ✓ should support --refs flag with multiple references  1594ms\\n     ✓ should maintain backward compatibility with positional ref  464ms\\n     ✓ should error when both positional ref and --refs are provided  467ms\\n     ✓ should continue processing after errors and report partial failures  1111ms\\n     ✓ should resolve refs using existing resolution logic (slugs, ULID prefixes)  2230ms\\n     ✓ should batch complete multiple tasks  1634ms\\n     ✓ should batch cancel multiple tasks  796ms\\n     ✓ should batch delete multiple tasks  661ms\\n ✓ tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts (8 tests) 152629ms\\n     ✓ does not spawn subagent when no pending_review tasks exist  441ms\\n     ✓ spawns subagent when pending_review tasks exist  30131ms\\n     ✓ detects newly-ready tasks when dependency is completed  811ms\\n     ✓ demonstrates stale vs fresh context difference  940ms\\n     ✓ processes pending_review task and continues loop  30117ms\\n     ✓ uses context to determine task eligibility  30090ms\\n     ✓ continues loop when subagent completes blocking task (AC-20 integration)  30010ms\\n     ✓ saves refreshed context to snapshot after pending_review processing  30087ms\\n\\n Test Files  1 failed | 158 passed (159)\\n      Tests  2 failed | 3523 passed | 3 skipped (3528)\\n   Start at  17:24:50\\n   Duration  153.09s (transform 11.10s, setup 0ms, import 21.26s, tests 1640.89s, environment 19ms)) failed in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts (normal/signal/crash cleanup paths). Posted MUST-FIX inline review on PR #586 and transitioned task to needs_work for fix cycle.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGXVE92ER5MGW40VNN3ZZR0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:29:48.579Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Fix cycle 1 started from PR #586 review feedback. Investigating regression in ralph session-budget integration tests and pending_review handling path.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGY1Z9AG1WYEX8CW0VMX05K\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:33:22.602Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Fix cycle 1 changes:\\n- Fixed task loading under KSPEC_SPEC_DIR override: loadAllTasks now treats spec-dir override as spec-only mode (same behavior as shadow mode) to prevent scanning parent directories and pulling unrelated temp task files.\\n- Fixed ralph pending-review escalation command from deprecated `task set-automation` to `task set --automation needs_review --reason ...`.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npm run build && npx vitest run tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts (15/15 passing)\\n- npm test (159 files, 3525 tests passing)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJHAD8E2QTA99YTNYCFCR9AT\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix: Truncate oversized ACP prompt payloads\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Ralph subagent and worker prompts embed raw JSON.stringify() of task/spec/session data inline. For large payloads (tasks with many notes, large specs), the resulting JSON-RPC line exceeds the Codex Rust binary read buffer, causing 'agent_client_protocol::rpc: failed to parse incoming message'. The parser receives a partial fragment and fails. Observed on the review subagent path, but the worker prompt has the same vulnerability.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-subagent-spawning\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"PR #590 reviewed and merged at head 690d0648\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"ralph\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T05:09:15.330Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:41:10.956Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:01:39.719Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:01:41.319Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJHAEBJXW166DHNWR5EMFZSF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T05:09:51.326Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Root Cause: Ralph prompts embed raw JSON.stringify() of task/spec/session data inline. For large payloads, the JSON-RPC line exceeds the Codex Rust binary read buffer causing parse failures. Approach: 32KB total prompt budget with largest-first truncation. Truncated sections show a blockquote notice with CLI fetch command and compact identity summary. Changes: (1) subagent.ts — SUBAGENT_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES, formatJsonSection(), truncatePromptIfNeeded(), compactSummary(). Updated buildSubagentPrompt(). (2) ralph.ts — Updated buildTaskWorkPrompt() with same helpers. (3) ralph/index.ts — Exported new helpers. (4) tests/ralph.test.ts — 14 new tests covering formatJsonSection, truncatePromptIfNeeded, and end-to-end buildSubagentPrompt truncation. (5) Spec ac-10 updated to reflect truncation behavior.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJMZYZR08RD00DZW1ACTRV0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T17:33:28.440Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Codex review on PR #590 found 2 MUST-FIX issues: (1) session-budget-integration test regression — 4/15 fail on branch vs 15/15 on main, though may be pre-existing flakiness tracked in @01KJGDR9; (2) AC annotation coverage gap for @ralph-subagent-spawning (9 of 13 ACs missing test annotations, mostly pre-existing).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJN05R8MPWDZRFTJFZ9NBVW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T17:33:35.369Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Codex PR review posted on #590 (pullrequestreview-3870620687). Two inline MUST-FIX comments:\\n1. src/ralph/subagent.ts:288 — session-budget-integration regression (4 test failures on branch, passes on main). Likely related to flaky timeout issue tracked in @01KJGDR9.\\n2. tests/ralph.test.ts:1680 — AC annotation coverage gap: only ac-2,9,10,11 annotated out of ac-1..13. Mostly pre-existing, not introduced by this PR.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJN2P73CJ748CQMEXTHA2J7\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T17:34:57.764Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Execution context:\\n- Background: PR #590 failed review due to session-budget-integration regressions and missing AC annotations for @ralph-subagent-spawning.\\n- Scope: stabilize session-budget integration behavior and add missing AC annotations for ac-1,3,4,5,6,7,8,12,13.\\n- Files: tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts, tests/ralph.test.ts, and minimal production code only if required by failing behavior.\\n- Verification: npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts; npm test -- tests/ralph.test.ts; npm test; kspec validate.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJPJ7HY6PW6N2N0F2XW82VB\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:00:55.615Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed MUST-FIX findings.\\n- Restored ralph timeout escalation command to current CLI shape: task set --automation needs_review --reason (replacing deprecated set-automation call).\\n- Added explicit AC annotations and integration coverage for @ralph-subagent-spawning ac-1,3,4,5,6,7,8,12,13 in ralph-context-refresh/ralph tests.\\n- Added mock ACP support for reviewer kickback path (MOCK_ACP_NEEDS_WORK_TASK) and verified task transitions to needs_work.\\n- Fixed session-budget integration harness isolation by removing KSPEC_SPEC_DIR override (it widened task discovery to /tmp and pulled unrelated pending_review fixtures).\\nVerification:\\n- npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts tests/ralph.test.ts (pass, 157 tests)\\n- npm test (fails in unrelated tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout; reproduced in isolation).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJQ8NTKQ46V5D7CMFTWTJA1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:13:11.123Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Codex PR review posted (pullrequestreview-3870655818). MUST-FIX: PR CI test shard 2 fails in tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts (assertions at lines 482 and 512). Root cause from CI logs: reviewer status/transition subprocess paths rely on bare 'kspec' and return null status in Actions context. Fix CLI invocation path in status-check helpers, then re-run CI.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJQVHMGYH4HCA79V7NEX8YM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:23:29.424Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Addressed PR review follow-up MUST-FIX items.\\n- Replaced hardcoded 'kspec' subprocess usage in ralph status/transition checks with portable Node CLI invocation (process.execPath + dist CLI path, optional KSPEC_CLI_PATH override).\\n- Hardened ralph-context-refresh integration assertions to verify task state transitions (completed/needs_work) instead of brittle log-string contracts.\\nVerification:\\n- npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts tests/ralph.test.ts (pass)\\n- npm run test:shard2 (pass; 1361 tests).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJRTTNYMD3QJ8W9QQYQZ8ZF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:40:34.494Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 6] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #590 is merge-conflicting with main (mergeable CONFLICTING / mergeStateStatus DIRTY). Rebase/resolve conflicts and rerun CI on latest HEAD.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJSCAPYPR6V25NXGCFQVF0Y\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T18:50:07.967Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Rebased fix/truncate-oversized-acp-prompts onto origin/main to resolve PR #590 merge conflict flagged by review subagent. No manual conflict edits were required. Re-verified after rebase:\\n- npm test -- tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts tests/ralph.test.ts (pass)\\n- npm run test:shard2 (pass)\\nPushed rebased branch with --force-with-lease.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJGJ17SR1GSXNK90DXKY4CR\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix merge driver non-interactive flag and improve conflict resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**Background**: Shadow branch diverged (170 local vs 260 remote commits). During merge, the merge driver was registered without --non-interactive, causing it to hang on stdin when conflicts were detected. This left files unmerged (ours version only), silently losing 12 task completions, notes, and remote-side spec changes.\\n\\n**Already done (this session):**\\n1. Diagnosed root cause: git config had `kspec merge-driver %O %A %B %P` but needed `--non-interactive` flag\\n2. Fixed local git config to include --non-interactive\\n3. Performed isolated rebase in /tmp worktree to produce correctly merged state\\n4. Applied corrected data as patch commit on kspec-meta (no force push needed)\\n5. Restored all 12 lost task completions with notes, verified 705 tasks intact\\n6. Marked 37 stale active sessions as abandoned, compacted all sessions (383MB reclaimed)\\n7. Created backup branches: kspec-meta-backup-2026-02-28 (pre-merge local), kspec-remote-pre-merge (pre-merge remote)\\n\\n**Still to do:**\\n1. Fix shadow.ts registration — ensure kspec init/setup always registers driver with --non-interactive\\n2. Add TTY detection fallback — merge driver should auto-detect when stdin is not a TTY and default to non-interactive mode (defense in depth)\\n3. Fix exit code behavior — in non-interactive mode, exit 0 even with conflicts (they're auto-resolved with ours-defaults + comments). Exit 1 breaks git rebase.\\n4. Improve notes array merging — when both sides modify notes, union by timestamp instead of picking one side. Notes are append-only logs.\\n5. Resolve inbox item about .kspec-agents-hash auto-resolution (01KJDFFJ)\\n6. Restore 8 lost notes on @01KJDQ11 (observations slug fix task) — local had detailed work log that was replaced by remote's 3 automated notes\\n7. Consider timestamp-aware conflict resolution for status fields (task state has natural ordering)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@yaml-merge-driver\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #601. Fixed merge driver: (1) shadow.ts validates/fixes stale config missing --non-interactive, (2) TTY detection auto-enables non-interactive when stdin is not TTY, (3) non-interactive mode exits 0 even with conflicts per spec ac-10. All tests pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"infra\",\n      \"bug\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:15:57.681Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:31:00.151Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:37:34.567Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:58:33.763Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJGJSC1QET01A4DV0TR5WYD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:16:22.402Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Session work completed (2026-02-28):\\n\\nRoot cause: merge driver registered without --non-interactive flag. When git invoked it on conflicting YAML files, it attempted interactive resolution via readline on unavailable stdin, hanging indefinitely. The ours file was never written with merged content, so git used unmodified ours version — silently losing remote-side changes.\\n\\nKey finding: merge driver has NO timestamp awareness — purely structural 3-way merge. For notes (append-only), it picks one side instead of unioning both.\\n\\nRebase approach worked: 170 local commits rebased onto 260 remote in isolated /tmp worktree. Auto-continue script handled non-YAML conflicts. All 169 commits applied. Result: 705 tasks with both sides preserved.\\n\\nOne data loss: Task @01KJDQ11 notes — 8 local notes replaced by 3 remote (ours-bias in rebase context). Backup branches available: kspec-meta-backup-2026-02-28 (local), kspec-remote-pre-merge (remote).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJH0155QWRXXC31YDA31HCJ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:23:36.357Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Refined scope — 3 code changes needed:\\n\\n1. src/parser/shadow.ts — Ensure all code paths that register merge.kspec.driver include --non-interactive. Audit initShadowBranch and any other registration points.\\n\\n2. src/cli/commands/merge-driver.ts — Two fixes:\\n   a. TTY detection: if process.stdin.isTTY is false, auto-enable non-interactive mode regardless of flag. Defense-in-depth so driver never hangs.\\n   b. Exit code: in non-interactive mode, exit 0 even with conflicts (line 536). Currently exits 1 which breaks git rebase. The spec ac-10 already says exit 0.\\n\\n3. src/merge/arrays.ts (mergeUlidArrays or equivalent) — Notes arrays should be union-merged by ULID, not fall through to scalar conflict. Spec ac-5 says 'notes never conflict' but the implementation doesn't match when arrays differ.\\n\\nItems from original description already done: lost notes on @01KJDQ11 restored, inbox item @01KJDFFJ is separate scope, timestamp-aware status resolution is a future enhancement.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHKEVS5G77Z1WYPKBHG165\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:34:12.986Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation changes (3 files):\\n\\n1. src/parser/shadow.ts — When existing merge driver config found in catch block, now validates --non-interactive flag is present. If missing (legacy registration), re-registers with --non-interactive. Ensures no stale config can cause hangs.\\n\\n2. src/cli/commands/merge-driver.ts (line 514) — Added TTY detection fallback: nonInteractive defaults to true when process.stdin.isTTY is false. Defense-in-depth so driver never hangs even if --non-interactive flag is somehow missing.\\n\\n3. src/cli/commands/merge-driver.ts (lines 534-536) — Non-interactive mode now always exits 0 regardless of conflicts. Per spec ac-10, conflicts are written as YAML comments and exit 0 prevents git from falling back to text merge (which corrupts YAML). Interactive mode retains exit 1 for unresolved conflicts.\\n\\nTests updated: 4 existing tests that expected exit code 1 for non-interactive conflicts now expect exit 0. All 12 merge-driver-cli tests pass.\\n\\nNote: Array merge (notes union by ULID) was already correctly implemented — no changes needed there. The spec ac-5 behavior was already working.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","status":"completed"}